hadiths[39]{hadithnumber,text}:
"24431","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Thumamah, who said: We went out with Fudalah ibn Ubayd to the land of the Romans, and he was an agent of Mu'awiyah over the pass. A cousin of ours was afflicted, and Fudalah prayed over him and stood over his grave until he buried him. When we had leveled his grave, he said: Lighten over him, for the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to command us to level the graves."
"24432","Muhammad ibn Ubayd narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Habib, from Abu Marzuq, from Fudalah al-Ansari: I heard him narrate that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to them on a day when he was fasting, and he called for a vessel containing water and drank. We said: O Messenger of Allah, this is a day you used to fast. He said: Yes, but I vomited."
"24433","Ya'qub narrated to us, my father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, from Yazid, he said: Thumamah ibn Shufay al-Hamdani narrated to me, he said: We raided the land of the Romans, with Fudalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari over that army. He mentioned the hadith and said: Fudalah said: Lighten, for I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanding the leveling of graves."
"24434","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' Humayd ibn Hani' informed me, from Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi, who narrated to me that he heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd, the Companion of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, heard a man supplicating in prayer without mentioning Allah, Mighty and Majestic, and without sending blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: This one has hastened. Then he called him and said to him and to others: When one of you prays, let him begin with praising his Lord and extolling Him, then let him send blessings upon the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, then let him supplicate afterwards with whatever he wishes."
"24435","Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Muqri' narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' informed me, from Amr ibn Malik, who narrated to him that he heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd say: When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, prayed with the people, men would fall from their standing posture during the prayer because of the privation upon them, and they were from the people of the Suffah, until the Bedouins would say: These are mad. When the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, finished the prayer, he would turn to them and say to them: If you knew what is for you with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, you would love to increase in need and poverty. Fudalah said: And I was with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that day."
"24436","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, and Ibn Lahi'ah, they said: Abu Hani' informed us, from Ali ibn Rabah, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, was brought a necklace containing gold and beads, being sold, and it was from the spoils. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, ordered that the gold in the necklace be removed by itself. Then he said: Gold for gold, weight for weight."
"24437","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' informed me, from Abu Ali al-Janbi, from Fudalah ibn Ubaydullah, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: The rider greets the walker, and the few greet the many."
"24438","Ibrahim ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me, that Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi informed him, that he heard Fudalah narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever dies upon one of these ranks will be resurrected upon it. Haywah said, meaning: ribat, hajj, or the like."
"24439","And al-Talaqani narrated it to us with this chain, from Ibn al-Mubarak, who said: The horseman greets the walker, the walker greets the standing one, and the few greet the many."
"24440","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' informed me, that Abu Ali Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi narrated the like of it."
"24441","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' informed me, that Abu Ali Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi narrated to him: Fudalah ibn Ubayd, from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Three, do not ask about them: a man who separates from the community, disobeys his imam, and dies disobedient; a female slave or a male slave who flees and dies; and a woman whose husband is absent while he has sufficed her the provision of this world, and she displays herself after him, do not ask about them. And three, do not ask about them: a man who disputes with Allah, Mighty and Majestic, over His cloak, for His cloak is pride and His garment is might; a man who doubts the affair of Allah; and the one who despairs of the mercy of Allah."
"24442","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' informed me, that Abu Ali informed him, that he heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that he heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Blessed is he who is guided to Islam, whose livelihood is sufficiency, and who is content."
"24443","Abu Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, Haywah narrated to us, and Ibn Lahi'ah, they said: Abu Hani' informed us, that Abu Ali al-Janbi narrated to him, that he heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: Whoever dies upon one of these ranks will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection."
"24444","Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami narrated to us, he said: I heard Hajjaj mention, from Makhul, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Muhayriz, who said: I said to Fudalah ibn Ubayd: What do you think about hanging the hand of the thief on the neck, is it from the Sunnah? He said: Yes. I saw the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, when a thief was brought to him: he ordered him, and his hand was cut off, then he ordered it and it was hung on his neck. Hajjaj said: And Fudalah was among those who pledged under the tree."
"24445","Abu Abd al-Rahman Abdullah ibn Ahmad said: I said to Yahya ibn Ma'in: Did you hear anything from Umar ibn Ali al-Muqaddami? He said: What did he have? I said: The hadith of Fudalah ibn Ubayd about hanging the hand. He said: No. Affan narrated it to us from him."
"24446","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim al-Talaqani narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from al-Awza'i, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah listens more attentively to the man with a beautiful voice reciting the Qur'an than the owner of the singing girl listens to her singing girl."
"24447","Yahya ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah informed us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abu Marzuq, from Hanash, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, woke up fasting, then called for a drink. One of his companions said to him: O Messenger of Allah, did you not wake up fasting? He said: Yes, but I vomited."
"24448","Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Abu Hani' narrated to me, from Abu Ali, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: The rider greets the walker, the walker greets the seated one, and the few greet the many."
"24449","Ishaq ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywah ibn Shurayh, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me, that Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi informed him, that he heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd narrating from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Whoever dies upon one of these ranks will be resurrected upon it on the Day of Resurrection. Haywah said, meaning: ribat, or hajj, or the like."
"24450","With this chain, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Every deceased person's deeds are sealed upon his deed except the one who dies guarding in the path of Allah, for his deeds grow for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is safe from the trial of the grave."
"24451","He said: And I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The mujahid is one who strives against his own self for Allah, or he said: concerning Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24452","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi al-Sa'bah, from Hanash, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever grows a white hair in the path of Allah, it will be a light for him on the Day of Resurrection. A man thereupon said: Some men pluck out white hair. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Whoever wishes, let him pluck out his light."
"24453","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Mu'awiyah ibn Sa'id al-Tujibi narrated to me, from one who narrated to him, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he said: The servant is safe from the punishment of Allah, Mighty and Majestic, as long as he seeks forgiveness from Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24454","Mu'awiyah ibn Amr narrated to us, Rishdin narrated to us, he said: Ibn Hani' al-Khawlani narrated to me, that Amr ibn Malik narrated to him, that he heard Fudalah say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Every deceased person's deeds are sealed upon his deed except the one guarding in the path of Allah: his reward continues for him until the Day of Resurrection, and he is protected from the trial of the grave."
"24455","Isam ibn Khalid al-Hadrami narrated to us, Safwan ibn Amr narrated to us, from Shurayh ibn Ubayd, that Fudalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari used to say: We raided with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, the raid of Tabuk, and the riding animals were under severe strain. They complained to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, about the strain upon their animals, so he waited for them at a narrow pass. The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, walked through it and said: Pass, in the name of Allah. The people passed over it with their animals, and he began to blow upon their animals: O Allah, carry upon them in Your path, for You carry upon the strong and the weak, upon the moist and the dry, on land and sea. He said: We had not reached Madinah before they began to contend with us for their reins. Fudalah said: This is the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, regarding the strong and the weak; so what about the moist and the dry? When we arrived in Sham, we raided the raid of Cyprus by sea, and when I saw the ships in the sea and what is loaded into them, I recognized the supplication of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"24456","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, he said: al-Awza'i narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Ubaydullah ibn Abi al-Muhajir, from Maysarah, the freedman of Fudalah, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, who said: Allah, Mighty and Majestic, listens more attentively to the man with a beautiful voice reciting the Qur'an than the owner of the singing girl listens to his singing girl."
"24457","Abu al-Yaman narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr, meaning Ibn Abi Maryam, narrated to us, from the elders, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari, who said: The Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, taught me a ruqyah and commanded me to treat with it whomever seemed fit to me. He said: Say: Our Lord is Allah who is in the heavens, sanctified is Your name; Your command is in heaven and earth. O Allah, as Your command is in heaven, so place Your mercy upon us on earth. O Allah, Lord of the good, forgive us our sins, our wrongs, and our faults, and send down a mercy from Your mercy and a healing from Your healing upon the complaint of so-and-so, and he will recover. He said: Say that three times, then seek refuge with the two Mu'awwidhatayn three times."
"24458","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Layth informed us, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed me, from Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi, he said: Fudalah ibn Ubayd narrated to me, he said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Shall I not inform you of the believer? The one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives. The Muslim is one from whose tongue and hand people are safe. The mujahid is one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah. And the emigrant is one who abandons faults and sins."
"24459","Al-Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said: Ibn Lahi'ah narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Abi Habib narrated to us, that Abu Ali al-Hamdani informed him that he saw Fudalah ibn Ubayd ordering that the graves of the Muslims in the land of the Romans be leveled, and he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: Level your graves with the ground."
"24460","Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from a man, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that they were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a raid. He said: And among us were two slaves, and he did not allot shares to them."
"24461","Abdullah ibn al-Walid narrated to us, he said: Sufyan informed us, and Muhammad ibn Kathir, the brother of Sulayman ibn Kathir, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from a man, from his father, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that they were with the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on a raid. He said: And among us were two slaves, and he did not allot shares to them."
"24462","Hashim and Yunus narrated to us, they said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us; Hashim said: Sa'id ibn Yazid Abu Shuja' narrated to us, and Yunus said: from Sa'id ibn Suwayd Abi Shuja' al-Himyari, from Khalid ibn Abi Imran, Yunus said: al-Ma'afiri, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari, who said: I bought a necklace on the day of the conquest of Khaybar for twelve dinars, containing gold and beads. I separated it and found in it more than twelve dinars. I mentioned that to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, and he said: It is not to be sold until it is separated."
"24463","Ya'qub narrated to us, he said: My father narrated to us, from Ibn Ishaq, he said: Yazid ibn Habib narrated to me, from Abu Marzuq, the freedman of Tujib, from Hanash, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd ibn Nafidh al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, came out to us on a day when he was fasting. He said: He called for water and drank. We said to him: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, this is a day you used to fast. He said: Yes, but I vomited."
"24464","Ya'mur ibn Bishr narrated to us, he said: Abdullah narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd informed us, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani narrated to me, from Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi, that Fudalah ibn Ubayd and Ubadah ibn al-Samit narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: When the Day of Resurrection comes and Allah, Most High, finishes judging the creation, two men will remain, and they will be ordered to the Fire. One of them will turn around, and the All-Compelling, blessed is His name, will say: Bring him back. They will bring him back, and it will be said to him: Why did you turn? Meaning, he will say: I had hoped that You would admit me into Paradise. He said: He will be ordered to Paradise, and he will say: My Lord, Mighty and Majestic, has given me so much that even if I were to feed the people of Paradise, that would not diminish what is with me at all. They said: And when the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, mentioned him, joy could be seen on his face."
"24465","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, he said: Abdullah, meaning Ibn al-Mubarak, informed us, he said: Haywah ibn Shurayh informed us, he said: Abu Hani' al-Khawlani informed us, that he heard Amr ibn Malik al-Janbi say: I heard Fudalah ibn Ubayd say: I heard the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, say: The mujahid is one who strives against his own self in the path of Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24466","Yahya ibn Ghaylan narrated to us, he said: al-Mufaddal ibn Fudalah narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Ayyash narrated to me, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, that he informed him, from Abu Marzuq, from Hanash al-San'ani, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd al-Ansari, from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that he was fasting, then he vomited and broke his fast."
"24467","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Rishdin ibn Sa'd narrated to me, from Humayd Abi Hani' al-Khawlani, from Amr ibn Malik, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said in the Farewell Pilgrimage: Shall I not inform you who the Muslim is? The one from whose tongue and hand the Muslims are safe. The believer is one whom people trust with their wealth and their lives. The emigrant is one who abandons faults and sins. And the mujahid is one who strives against his own self in obedience to Allah, Mighty and Majestic."
"24468","Qutaybah ibn Sa'id narrated to us, he said: Layth ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from Ubaydullah ibn Abi Ja'far, from al-Julah Abi Kathir, he said: Hanash al-San'ani narrated to me, from Fudalah ibn Ubayd, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, on the day of Khaybar, trading with the Jews an uqiyyah of gold for two or three dinars. The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said: Do not sell gold for gold except weight for weight."
"24469","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said: al-Jurayri informed me, from Abdullah ibn Buraydah, that a man from the companions of the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, traveled to Fudalah ibn Ubayd while he was in Egypt. He came to him while he was leading a camel of his. He said: I did not come to you as a visitor; I came to you only for a hadith that reached me from the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, hoping that you have knowledge of it. He saw him disheveled and said: Why do I see you disheveled when you are the ruler of the land? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, used to forbid us from much luxury. And he saw him barefoot and said: Why do I see you barefoot? He said: The Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, commanded us to go barefoot sometimes."
